WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:07.069
The Home tab is where a designer gets the whole workspace into view, without surrendering the choices that shape the work.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:17.426
The rail keeps every stage close: build from Venue Magic, return to presentations and the content library, then measure what clients actually opened.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:27.774
Across the top, the live totals show 28 presentations, 18 client links, and 183 opens. They are signals, not instructions.

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:36.347
When it’s time to begin, choose the starting point that fits the assignment: a venue-led story, a DealDeck, or a partner page.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:44.377
The recent list keeps active work visible. Search when the library grows, scan each status, then open the presentation that deserves attention.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:51.720
Analytics sits beside every item, so the team can review response before deciding what to refine or share next.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:58.369
That is the Home tab: one clear view of the work, with the designer still deciding what moves forward.
